WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.660
Almost 100 Russian missiles hit three key bridges, killing people and closing the capital's roots. This is Omni View Top World News, Episode 59. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After the capital, a declaration in Chen Zhen, talks in Brussels, and a budget vote in Ottawa, then the case on both sides and a sign of progress. President Volodymyr Zelensky called that overnight assault one of the war's most massive, the BBC reports, and put the dead at eight or more.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.920
while the BBC's own figure was five.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.100
The Air Force said about 400 drones flew with the missiles,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.660
and spokesman Yuri Ignaut ranked the night

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.980
among the most powerful yet.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.940
Traffic is shut on the Podilsko-Voskarsensky,

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.820
Darnitsky and Southern Bridges.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.460
Mayor Vitaly Klitschko told people to stay

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.620
out of the city by car unless they had to come,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.640
and said a critical facility was hit

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.260
and seven medical staff were hurt.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.600
Prime Minister Sergei Kuretskiy counted 28 injured

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.580
across nine regions, including an ambulance hospital

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:03.440
in Karkiv. In Lviv, Mayor Andrii Sadovi said two people died at the Skneel of railway station

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:09.060
and ten were hurt, with rescuers still on sight. Over the border, Defense Minister Vladislav

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:14.820
Kosiniyat Kamish said a Russian cruise missile came down about 50 kilometers, 31 miles, inside

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.320
Poland, and that two more projectiles fell in nearby villages without injuring anyone.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:25.080
Polish and Swedish jets went up and have since stood down. President Vladimir Putin had promised

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.920
to reply to Ukraine's Crimean bridge strike that would be far more painful.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.860
Zelensky said that bridge operation took weeks.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.400
The barrage started hours after Andy Burnham, Emmanuel Macron, and Friedrich Murds, said

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.940
they were ready to negotiate with Moscow, while the Kremlin rejected a U.S. claim that Russia

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.840
might accept Western-backed security guarantees for Ukraine.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.020
Onvoid Jared Kushner said Washington wants to deal with Europe beside it.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.780
China hosted a three-way summit in Chen-gen on Thursday, and the Hawaii Tribune Herald reports

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.100
that the United States, China and Russia

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.160
signed a symbolic peace declaration there.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.020
They restated that a nuclear war cannot be won

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.160
and must never be fought.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.760
They also promised United Nations reforms,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.540
more fuel for every country

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.500
and immunity for state officials and international courts,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.640
plus talks on nuclear risk with no calendar attached.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.280
The text is silent on Russia's war in Ukraine

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.140
and on the American conflict with Iran.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.600
It does not start the three-way arms-cut

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.800
Donald Trump has wanted,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.000
which Beijing has refused because it says

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.620
its arsenal is smaller. Vladimir Putin said the paper sets no ambitious goals and that no one will

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:35.520
be forced to follow it. Trump called Putin his friend, took a hug from Xi Jinping, told NBC the

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.740
session was a 12 out of 10, and told Reuters it was bigger than Yalta. He said he would rather have

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:45.760
people holding 4,000 nuclear weapons as friends than as enemies, and that giving the weapons up

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:51.660
is not easy. Foreign Minister Wang Yi said working-level contact will continue. Trump scheduled a

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.400
Washington News conference for noon today. Reuters judged the Asia trip short on concrete

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.664
winds, whatever the boasts of history. Brussels is where Andy Burnham sat down on Friday

00:03:01.664 --> 00:03:06.544
with Antonio Costa and Ursula Von Der Lyon, and the Globe and Mail reports this is only

00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:12.464
the second UK EU summit since Britain left. On offer, up to 100,000 young adults each

00:03:12.464 --> 00:03:17.084
way, living and working across the divide for as long as three years, a shared emissions

00:03:17.084 --> 00:03:20.004
market, and an end to checks on food and farm goods.

00:03:20.464 --> 00:03:24.524
Burnham said that could add half a percent to the British economy, a tenth of a point

00:03:24.524 --> 00:03:28.784
above his earlier estimate, and he pointed to Treasury analysis for the same ceiling,

00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:31.304
calling it this Parliament's biggest growth move.

00:03:31.824 --> 00:03:36.224
An EU official who would not be named said the package dies unless tuition fees are settled

00:03:36.224 --> 00:03:37.184
within six months.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:41.984
Brussels wants European students in Britain on domestic rates, not the foreign rate,

00:03:42.324 --> 00:03:43.544
and London has resisted.

00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:48.504
The Guardian was told by EU sources that linking food access to those fees is how the block

00:03:48.504 --> 00:03:53.124
cancels leverage Britain would get from a six-month pause on tuition, while London chases

00:03:53.124 --> 00:03:56.344
a seat in mating Europe rules built against Chinese supply chains.

00:03:56.844 --> 00:03:59.884
France has insisted Britain get no vote on food and drink law.

00:04:00.424 --> 00:04:02.544
Talks on the manufacturing rules are still open.

00:04:03.064 --> 00:04:06.604
The price of the deals is accepting some EU standards Britain does not write.

00:04:07.064 --> 00:04:11.884
Burnham has called rejoining one option among others, not a near prospect, and one that

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.284
would need British voters in every EU capital.

00:04:14.844 --> 00:04:19.784
Vonder Layon asked for youth chances, easier agri-food trade, and tighter economic security.

00:04:20.384 --> 00:04:22.944
Burnham sold the package as lower supermarket prices.

00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:27.055
Canada's House of Commons has passed the 2026 budget.

00:04:27.495 --> 00:04:33.815
Global news reports, 162 votes to 151, on a plan tabled November 5th.

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:38.135
It borrows billions in rewrites taxes mainly to build infrastructure and other capital

00:04:38.135 --> 00:04:43.575
works, including a $36 billion productivity deduction aimed at getting firms to buy machinery.

00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:48.115
The Liberals now have a majority, built from by-elections and floor crossings.

00:04:48.595 --> 00:04:53.415
Last year, Elizabeth May's green vote decided it, with two new Democrats and two conservatives

00:04:53.415 --> 00:04:54.655
abstaining or absent.

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:59.795
Pierre Poilierre says the borrowing dumps costs on Canadians and does not make life cheaper.

00:05:00.455 --> 00:05:04.595
Budget officer Annette Ryan flagged how much is being borrowed, then found the government

00:05:04.595 --> 00:05:09.555
narrowly inside its fiscal anchors, helped since spring by oil prices in stronger revenue.

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:13.795
Finance Minister Francois Philippe Champagne said confident countries invest,

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:18.715
and that Canada is one of the few in the G7 that can fund growth and affordability together.

00:05:19.375 --> 00:05:23.475
Avilouis said his new Democrats would oppose a budget he thinks is written for big business,

00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:26.735
not for groceries, phones, housing, or health care.

00:05:27.275 --> 00:05:32.135
Eve Francois Blanchett attacked the title Matrix-Shayneux, saying Quebec does not gain control

00:05:32.135 --> 00:05:35.715
role of its own affairs. Committee can still amend the implementation bills.

00:05:36.195 --> 00:05:41.295
The second implementation act from the 2025 budget, tabled in May, is still in Parliament.

00:05:42.379 --> 00:05:47.759
France has a new name in the 2027 presidential field. Dominique DeVille-Pen, a former prime

00:05:47.759 --> 00:05:53.339
minister, declared on Friday, France 24 reports, at the Maison de la Merrie, Latine in Paris.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:58.879
His team cast him against the National Rally, France Unbowed, and the Macronis Center. Three

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:01.879
forces he says are cutting the country apart and causing its decay.

00:06:02.439 --> 00:06:06.179
He told voters not to accept a death foretold, and called himself renewal.

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:08.119
The party is humanist France.

00:06:08.619 --> 00:06:13.119
He has a book out, a larger social media presence, and a speaking tour behind more than two

00:06:13.119 --> 00:06:14.079
years of preparation.

00:06:14.679 --> 00:06:20.079
The team says 300 mayors have pledged signatures toward the 500 required to stand, the bar that

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.179
stopped him in 2012.

00:06:21.679 --> 00:06:26.439
He strategized for Jacques Chiroc from the 1980s, was foreign minister when France opposed

00:06:26.439 --> 00:06:31.979
the U.S.-led invasion of Iraq in 2003, and has never won an election. Opposition to

00:06:31.979 --> 00:06:36.219
Israel's campaign in Gaza has brought him notice from younger, more left-leaning voters

00:06:36.219 --> 00:06:41.869
who once would not have considered him. In Iraq, a compromise France 24 reported, with

00:06:41.869 --> 00:06:46.429
the Iran-backed militia Kataiyab-Hesbola, was expected to let government forces enter

00:06:46.429 --> 00:06:52.129
Jurf al-Sakhar on Friday over alleged state oil smuggling. A Pakistani minister is in

00:06:52.129 --> 00:06:57.549
India for the first time since the 2025 war, Al Jazeera reports, and both capitals insist

00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:59.429
the visit states strictly multilateral.

00:06:59.969 --> 00:07:04.429
Democrats who are due to take the United States Congress are split, CBS News reports,

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:08.949
over whether the December 11 funding deadline should restrict money for the Iran War.

00:07:09.469 --> 00:07:13.909
A jury in Britain convicted four men of sexually assaulting Joanne Young, the New York Times

00:07:13.909 --> 00:07:17.729
reports, and rejected their claim that her husband had told them she consented.

00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:22.629
Thailand has opened its market to pork from the United States, and Bloomberg says that

00:07:22.629 --> 00:07:24.209
raises the risk for Thai farmers.

00:07:25.193 --> 00:07:29.593
On the reset with Europe, the case on both sides turns on whether Britain should live under

00:07:29.593 --> 00:07:34.293
rules it does not write, and settle what EU students pay before food and youth deals

00:07:34.293 --> 00:07:34.793
can start.

00:07:35.433 --> 00:07:39.593
Andy Burnham says the Brexit Britain was given has not worked, and that the country lost

00:07:39.593 --> 00:07:40.373
more than it gained.

00:07:40.933 --> 00:07:45.373
He argues a closer partnership is good for working people, good for Britain, and good for

00:07:45.373 --> 00:07:48.133
Europe, because costs fall and the young get chances.

00:07:48.613 --> 00:07:52.493
He told businesses and Brussels the sides were pretty much there and the deal was really

00:07:52.493 --> 00:07:57.473
good, and he has left every future option open, including a return to the block, while

00:07:57.473 --> 00:08:00.473
saying that reversal is only one outcome and is not close.

00:08:01.233 --> 00:08:06.233
Nigel Farage told the BBC he is afraid the great Brexit debate has just started again, and

00:08:06.233 --> 00:08:09.553
that it soon becomes a plain choice, rejoin or stay out.

00:08:10.073 --> 00:08:14.473
Supporters of Brexit say taking rules London does not set, undoes the independence the

00:08:14.473 --> 00:08:15.313
leave vote was for.

00:08:15.753 --> 00:08:17.813
European sources call it a hard bargain.

00:08:18.373 --> 00:08:20.073
Tying food access to the fee fight

00:08:20.073 --> 00:08:22.533
is how they blunt leverage Britain would otherwise hold.

00:08:22.973 --> 00:08:25.613
And France has insisted the UK get no vote on food

00:08:25.613 --> 00:08:26.253
and drink law.

00:08:26.733 --> 00:08:28.793
The next month's decide whether that fee fight

00:08:28.793 --> 00:08:30.393
and the fight over who writes the rules

00:08:30.393 --> 00:08:32.013
finish the reset or stall it.

00:08:33.022 --> 00:08:35.602
A pill named Darax on Rossib is a sign of progress

00:08:35.602 --> 00:08:37.182
in a trial the Guardian describes.

00:08:37.822 --> 00:08:41.002
61 people, newly diagnosed with pancreatic cancer

00:08:41.002 --> 00:08:42.782
that had already spread, took it.

00:08:42.782 --> 00:08:46.162
In one of every 12, the cancer could no longer be detected.

00:08:46.562 --> 00:08:49.582
In nearly every person enrolled, the tumors quit growing.

00:08:50.082 --> 00:08:53.822
The paper says the result is being hailed as the biggest treatment breakthrough for this

00:08:53.822 --> 00:08:54.682
cancer in decades.

